1
00:00:06,423 --> 00:00:09,926
[heartbeat whooshing through machine]

2
00:00:10,010 --> 00:00:14,431
[whooshing continues]

3
00:00:18,226 --> 00:00:19,686
[phone buzzes]

4
00:00:19,769 --> 00:00:22,689
[heartbeat continues]

5
00:00:23,815 --> 00:00:25,400
All right, we're done.

6
00:00:25,483 --> 00:00:26,526
[machine beeps]

7
00:00:28,987 --> 00:00:30,864
Is everything okay?

8
00:00:31,406 --> 00:00:34,367
Make an appointment with your cardiologist
as soon as possible.

9
00:00:34,993 --> 00:00:36,953
[ominous music playing]

10
00:00:37,954 --> 00:00:39,080
[door closes]

11
00:00:41,916 --> 00:00:47,839
[dramatic music playing]

12
00:00:48,923 --> 00:00:51,259
[Teagan] Mom, the shower's broken.

13
00:00:51,342 --> 00:00:53,428
I know, I'm working on it.

14
00:00:53,511 --> 00:00:56,848
It's just, we have to move
from well water to the town plumbing,

15
00:00:56,931 --> 00:00:59,225
and this is a heritage house,
so we need a permit.

16
00:00:59,309 --> 00:01:01,895
-Mine just got rejected.
-How long is that gonna take?

17
00:01:01,978 --> 00:01:04,022
{\an8}-I have to shower.
-Use my deodorant spray.

18
00:01:04,105 --> 00:01:05,398
{\an8}-It'll buy you a day or two.
-Mom.

19
00:01:06,024 --> 00:01:08,777
{\an8}-That can't be the solution.
-There's a board of appeals.

20
00:01:08,860 --> 00:01:13,490
{\an8}Oh! I have an in with the state senator,
DeeDee Garner.

21
00:01:13,573 --> 00:01:16,785
{\an8}-We used to do the pageant circuit.
-That's Baloo and Britney's mom.

22
00:01:16,868 --> 00:01:17,786
{\an8}Are you friends?

23
00:01:17,869 --> 00:01:20,830
{\an8}Friends with one of them,
the other wants me dead.

24
00:01:20,914 --> 00:01:22,248
{\an8}What about you with DeeDee?

25
00:01:22,332 --> 00:01:23,666
{\an8}Oh, wants me dead too.

26
00:01:23,750 --> 00:01:26,461
{\an8}But I mean, it's been so long,
it's probably fine.

27
00:01:26,961 --> 00:01:29,881
{\an8}And if not, I will carve out a budget
for dry shampoo.

28
00:01:31,466 --> 00:01:33,176
{\an8}[Teagan] Teagan says pull.

29
00:01:36,971 --> 00:01:38,348
Teagan says freeze.

30
00:01:39,474 --> 00:01:42,185
-Where's Josh? Why isn't he here?
-I dunno, I haven't heard from him.

31
00:01:42,268 --> 00:01:43,853
So practice is optional now.

32
00:01:44,813 --> 00:01:45,897
Row.

33
00:01:45,980 --> 00:01:47,607
-Teagan says.
-Crap.

34
00:01:48,608 --> 00:01:50,193
Teagan says pull.

35
00:01:51,444 --> 00:01:52,821
Okay.

36
00:01:53,321 --> 00:01:54,948
Teagan says, rate up for a beat.

37
00:01:58,868 --> 00:02:01,162
Teagan says, give me a "Yes, ma'am!"

38
00:02:01,246 --> 00:02:02,664
[all] Yes, ma'am!

39
00:02:03,456 --> 00:02:04,749
[Teagan] Okay.

40
00:02:08,253 --> 00:02:09,504
Coming for stroke.

41
00:02:10,004 --> 00:02:12,298
You give it your best shot.

42
00:02:12,382 --> 00:02:14,259
You might be the fastest,
but it'll never happen.

43
00:02:14,342 --> 00:02:15,885
Don't be so sure about that.

44
00:02:16,594 --> 00:02:18,638
No one's gonna follow a faid over a Regis.

45
00:02:20,598 --> 00:02:22,183
[somber music playing]

46
00:02:24,185 --> 00:02:25,311
[Teagan] Cam.

47
00:02:25,395 --> 00:02:29,357
I have been promised tacos,
and I've come to collect.

48
00:02:30,441 --> 00:02:31,776
[both laugh quietly]

49
00:02:32,360 --> 00:02:33,278
Is everything okay?

50
00:02:33,361 --> 00:02:36,281
Get ready for some tacos
that will change your life.

51
00:02:36,364 --> 00:02:39,909
[laughing] Oh, wow,
I'm from SoCal. I highly doubt that.

52
00:02:41,369 --> 00:02:42,495
[Baloo] What's this?

53
00:02:42,579 --> 00:02:45,456
[intriguing music playing]

54
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:48,376
[singsong] Oh, Ryder!

55
00:02:48,459 --> 00:02:49,836
Got a box for you.

56
00:02:54,382 --> 00:02:56,467
"You have stolen my heart."

57
00:02:56,968 --> 00:03:00,096
"Will you go to the Fall Formal with me?
From Amber."

58
00:03:00,180 --> 00:03:01,097
[Baloo] Aw.

59
00:03:01,181 --> 00:03:04,475
Hold on, so she's giving you a heart
and then saying you stole it?

60
00:03:04,559 --> 00:03:06,936
Which is it?
And why does it look like a ransom note?

61
00:03:07,020 --> 00:03:09,731
Can you guys not ruin the magic
of this promposal right now?

62
00:03:09,814 --> 00:03:12,901
Wait, is it really a promposal
if it's for the Fall Formal?

63
00:03:12,984 --> 00:03:16,029
-Is it more like a form-posal?
-That's not better.

64
00:03:16,112 --> 00:03:18,615
Well, it looks like
I got a date to the Fall Formal.

65
00:03:18,698 --> 00:03:20,700
I'll organize the table for the dance.
Who's coming?

66
00:03:20,783 --> 00:03:23,369
Baloo, you bringing Thirst Trap Guy?

67
00:03:23,453 --> 00:03:24,454
Uh…

68
00:03:25,163 --> 00:03:27,040
Didn't pan out. Just me this year.

69
00:03:28,666 --> 00:03:31,085
Showing up at the end of practice,
that's a choice.

70
00:03:31,169 --> 00:03:33,546
Dentist appointment.
Cleared it with Coach.

71
00:03:33,630 --> 00:03:35,298
Getting my workout in now.

72
00:03:35,798 --> 00:03:37,759
Glad we could work around your schedule.

73
00:03:38,635 --> 00:03:39,510
[boy clearing throat]

74
00:03:39,594 --> 00:03:40,678
[school bell ringing]

75
00:03:42,263 --> 00:03:43,514
[indistinct chatter]

76
00:03:45,808 --> 00:03:47,268
I'll catch up with you outside.

77
00:03:47,352 --> 00:03:48,645
Okay.

78
00:03:51,564 --> 00:03:53,024
Time to talk.

79
00:03:53,107 --> 00:03:55,026
Okay, let's talk.

80
00:03:55,610 --> 00:03:58,988
Wanna explain your sudden pivot
from being just friends?

81
00:03:59,072 --> 00:04:02,075
-I thought that part was pretty clear.
-I thought we were gonna let this go.

82
00:04:02,158 --> 00:04:04,953
-What if I didn't want to?
-What if you made yourself do it anyway?

83
00:04:05,995 --> 00:04:08,248
I don't know
that I'm supposed to be with Britney.

84
00:04:08,957 --> 00:04:11,584
Come on, Josh,
you guys are perfect for each other.

85
00:04:11,668 --> 00:04:13,544
You're both the worst people that I know.

86
00:04:15,713 --> 00:04:19,592
Yeah, I don't think she'd like me
if I wasn't… this.

87
00:04:20,093 --> 00:04:21,594
What's going on with you?

88
00:04:23,054 --> 00:04:24,514
I, uh…

89
00:04:26,808 --> 00:04:28,059
Uh…

90
00:04:28,142 --> 00:04:29,644
It's nothing. I-it's fine.

91
00:04:29,727 --> 00:04:32,272
Whatever's happening in your life,

92
00:04:32,355 --> 00:04:35,441
I'm not going to be the excuse
to run away from it.

93
00:04:35,525 --> 00:04:37,193
You have to deal with it.

94
00:04:39,153 --> 00:04:41,489
Hey, you have so much, Josh.

95
00:04:41,990 --> 00:04:43,449
So just…

96
00:04:44,284 --> 00:04:47,203
before you throw everything away,
take a look at what you'd be losing.

97
00:04:59,382 --> 00:05:01,551
Hey, you're Madison, right?

98
00:05:02,051 --> 00:05:04,470
-Is your dad around?
-Yeah, he's just prepping for the dance.

99
00:05:04,554 --> 00:05:05,430
Can I help you?

100
00:05:05,513 --> 00:05:08,683
Teagan forgot her homework assignment,
and I thought I'd drop it off.

101
00:05:08,766 --> 00:05:11,144
-You could just leave it with me.
-I don't mind waiting.

102
00:05:13,104 --> 00:05:15,940
Let me save you some time.
I've seen this before.

103
00:05:16,024 --> 00:05:18,318
The drop by, the smile, the coffee.

104
00:05:18,401 --> 00:05:20,320
You're not the first PTA mom to come by.

105
00:05:21,070 --> 00:05:22,864
But it never happens. He's not looking.

106
00:05:22,947 --> 00:05:27,243
No, that's not what this is.
I'm just… Your dad and I are old friends.

107
00:05:28,328 --> 00:05:29,329
Sure.

108
00:05:32,248 --> 00:05:33,458
You know what?

109
00:05:34,375 --> 00:05:35,376
I'll leave this here.

110
00:05:40,131 --> 00:05:43,051
-Hey! Hi.
-Ella, hey. What are you doing here?

111
00:05:43,134 --> 00:05:46,804
I had to drop off Teagan's homework,
and I thought I'd give you one of these.

112
00:05:46,888 --> 00:05:48,890
From Discovery, my favorite spot.

113
00:05:49,891 --> 00:05:51,642
[Ella] Oat milk latte, extra shot.

114
00:05:51,726 --> 00:05:53,561
Thank you. I could really use this.

115
00:05:53,644 --> 00:05:57,523
FYI, he prefers decaf after 9.
I gotta move this gear.

116
00:05:57,607 --> 00:05:58,524
[Hayden laughs quietly]

117
00:06:01,694 --> 00:06:02,862
It was nice to meet you.

118
00:06:02,945 --> 00:06:03,946
[Madison] Mm-hmm.

119
00:06:04,572 --> 00:06:05,782
Love you.

120
00:06:06,324 --> 00:06:07,367
Yeah.

121
00:06:07,450 --> 00:06:10,370
-Well, Madison seems a little…
-Intense. It's her default mode.

122
00:06:10,453 --> 00:06:12,121
-Okay.
-Always running interference.

123
00:06:12,205 --> 00:06:15,375
She's more bark than bite though,
I promise you.

124
00:06:16,376 --> 00:06:18,503
So what are you up to Saturday night?
Dinner?

125
00:06:18,586 --> 00:06:21,047
I have to work at the Crab Shack.
How about Friday?

126
00:06:21,130 --> 00:06:24,926
Can't do Friday.
I am chaperoning the formal.

127
00:06:25,009 --> 00:06:26,594
Actually, we could use some help.

128
00:06:26,677 --> 00:06:29,013
No, you lost me at chaperone.

129
00:06:29,097 --> 00:06:32,558
What, trying to police
100 hormonal teenagers not fun?

130
00:06:32,642 --> 00:06:34,644
What about hanging with other chaperones,

131
00:06:34,727 --> 00:06:36,771
including your personal favorite,
DeeDee Garner?

132
00:06:38,439 --> 00:06:39,440
DeeDee Garner?

133
00:06:39,524 --> 00:06:40,566
Uh-huh.

134
00:06:41,401 --> 00:06:43,277
Uh, you know what? Sign me up.

135
00:06:43,861 --> 00:06:45,613
I didn't know you two kept in touch.

136
00:06:45,696 --> 00:06:48,116
We didn't, but it's time for a reunion.

137
00:06:48,616 --> 00:06:49,909
[knocking]

138
00:06:50,535 --> 00:06:53,704
Hey, coach duty calls.
See you at the dance.

139
00:06:55,790 --> 00:06:58,918
Ryder Regis, come on in.
What's on your mind?

140
00:06:59,001 --> 00:07:01,003
Big news, actually.

141
00:07:01,087 --> 00:07:04,215
I had a video chat with the coach
from the Dartmouth rowing program,

142
00:07:04,298 --> 00:07:06,717
and he invited me
to the campus next Tuesday.

143
00:07:07,718 --> 00:07:10,596
-It's cool if I miss practice, right?
-No, I need my stroke seat there.

144
00:07:10,680 --> 00:07:12,390
You'll have to find another day to go.

145
00:07:12,473 --> 00:07:15,309
You let Josh miss a day,
but I can't do what I have to do?

146
00:07:15,393 --> 00:07:16,894
Josh had a dental issue.

147
00:07:16,978 --> 00:07:19,147
-It's preferential treatment.
-It really isn't.

148
00:07:19,230 --> 00:07:21,441
It's my team, so my call.

149
00:07:23,818 --> 00:07:27,780
[pensive music playing]

150
00:07:34,912 --> 00:07:35,955
Wow.

151
00:07:36,038 --> 00:07:37,081
Hi, babe.

152
00:07:38,666 --> 00:07:39,959
I have a surprise for you.

153
00:07:40,042 --> 00:07:41,919
I can see that.

154
00:07:42,003 --> 00:07:44,172
It's a recreation of our first date.

155
00:07:44,255 --> 00:07:46,632
When you took me
to that perfect chalet in Rhône Valley.

156
00:07:47,341 --> 00:07:49,010
I had our faves flown in.

157
00:07:49,093 --> 00:07:52,221
Macarons from La Bissette,
éclairs from La Lyonnaise.

158
00:07:52,305 --> 00:07:55,308
-And the opera cake from--
-From Sabine's.

159
00:07:55,391 --> 00:07:57,101
[giggles] I knew you'd remember.

160
00:07:57,185 --> 00:07:58,895
But why the trip down memory lane?

161
00:07:58,978 --> 00:08:00,813
You're promposing to me, silly.

162
00:08:00,897 --> 00:08:04,233
I know you've had a lot going on
with your family and Ryder.

163
00:08:04,317 --> 00:08:07,528
So I thought I'd plan it for you,
especially since there's a photo shoot.

164
00:08:07,612 --> 00:08:09,197
Over here, thank you.

165
00:08:09,280 --> 00:08:10,948
-Oh, uh…
-[Britney laughs]

166
00:08:11,032 --> 00:08:13,284
Your grandfather always loved
<i>Bespoke Magazine</i>.

167
00:08:13,367 --> 00:08:15,870
Well, they're featuring us in a spread.

168
00:08:15,953 --> 00:08:17,914
-[camera clicking]
-How did you swing that?

169
00:08:17,997 --> 00:08:20,666
I pitched them an article
about a next-gen power couple,

170
00:08:20,750 --> 00:08:22,502
which will build my public profile.

171
00:08:22,585 --> 00:08:24,295
[Josh] This is amazing.

172
00:08:24,378 --> 00:08:25,296
The article starts

173
00:08:25,379 --> 00:08:28,341
with how we were voted
King and Queen of the Fall Formal.

174
00:08:28,424 --> 00:08:29,675
-Really?
-Mm-hmm.

175
00:08:29,759 --> 00:08:31,219
Congrats, babe.

176
00:08:31,302 --> 00:08:33,930
To us. We are a great team.

177
00:08:34,597 --> 00:08:37,058
I provide the publicity,
the political power,

178
00:08:37,141 --> 00:08:39,977
you the pedigree and charisma,

179
00:08:40,061 --> 00:08:41,103
not to mention the abs.

180
00:08:41,187 --> 00:08:43,189
-[both laugh]
-[uneasy music playing]

181
00:08:46,442 --> 00:08:47,443
Come here.

182
00:08:49,487 --> 00:08:54,492
[camera clicking]

183
00:08:54,575 --> 00:08:57,537
-[Teagan] Oh!
-[Cam] It's got a kick. So?

184
00:09:01,707 --> 00:09:04,085
-Solid B plus.
-B plus?

185
00:09:04,168 --> 00:09:07,838
It's a great grade. Way above average
for East Coast Mexican food.

186
00:09:07,922 --> 00:09:09,715
-I'm offended.
-I'm from LA.

187
00:09:09,799 --> 00:09:12,593
-I have loyalties.
-Okay.

188
00:09:13,594 --> 00:09:14,804
[Teagan] Ow!

189
00:09:14,887 --> 00:09:15,888
Are you okay?

190
00:09:15,972 --> 00:09:20,226
Yeah, I just… I hit a blister
from my last erg session.

191
00:09:20,309 --> 00:09:21,936
-Oh yeah, that's a beaut.
-[Teagan laughs]

192
00:09:22,019 --> 00:09:24,355
-I popped a good one yesterday right here.
-[Teagan] Oh!

193
00:09:24,438 --> 00:09:26,315
That one is not messing around.

194
00:09:26,399 --> 00:09:29,151
I know you're supposed to leave them
alone because of infection, but…

195
00:09:29,235 --> 00:09:30,236
I can't row with it.

196
00:09:30,319 --> 00:09:33,573
I keep meaning to deal with mine,
but I can't with my left hand.

197
00:09:33,656 --> 00:09:36,325
-I can take care of it if you want.
-Really?

198
00:09:36,409 --> 00:09:38,452
It doesn't bother me
if it doesn't bother you.

199
00:09:39,287 --> 00:09:41,539
Come on, I got a first aid kit inside.

200
00:09:45,418 --> 00:09:46,419
Okay.

201
00:09:51,757 --> 00:09:56,012
Not quite how I expected
this date to go down, but…

202
00:09:56,095 --> 00:09:57,221
Yup.

203
00:09:57,305 --> 00:09:58,931
[soft music playing]

204
00:10:00,808 --> 00:10:01,809
Ready?

205
00:10:04,687 --> 00:10:05,688
Okay.

206
00:10:08,232 --> 00:10:09,775
So attractive.

207
00:10:09,859 --> 00:10:11,444
[both laughing]

208
00:10:11,527 --> 00:10:13,446
It's the life of a rower.

209
00:10:13,529 --> 00:10:16,240
My mom always asks me
why I'm obsessed with crew,

210
00:10:16,324 --> 00:10:18,034
but I never know how to explain it.

211
00:10:18,534 --> 00:10:20,453
It's not an obsession. It's just…

212
00:10:21,537 --> 00:10:22,663
who I am.

213
00:10:24,081 --> 00:10:25,082
Same.

214
00:10:25,750 --> 00:10:28,753
It's where I feel the most… like me.

215
00:10:30,796 --> 00:10:32,423
Okay, I know this sounds crazy,

216
00:10:32,506 --> 00:10:35,760
but when I watch the Olympics,
I keep thinking…

217
00:10:36,552 --> 00:10:39,513
I can do that. You know,
that's where I'm supposed to be.

218
00:10:40,097 --> 00:10:42,350
Even if I'm just
some guy from Eagle's Cove.

219
00:10:44,518 --> 00:10:46,187
I just need people to believe in me.

220
00:10:47,438 --> 00:10:48,689
They do.

221
00:10:49,482 --> 00:10:50,650
Not really.

222
00:10:51,150 --> 00:10:52,985
No one sees me in stroke.

223
00:10:53,486 --> 00:10:57,073
If I can't win them over,
I don't stand a chance.

224
00:10:58,532 --> 00:10:59,825
How do you do it?

225
00:11:00,326 --> 00:11:03,245
You got them to listen.
I mean, you even got a "Yes, ma'am."

226
00:11:03,329 --> 00:11:06,832
-You want a "Yes, ma'am"?
-Yeah, who doesn't want a "Yes, ma'am"?

227
00:11:07,375 --> 00:11:11,128
But seriously… What am I doing wrong?

228
00:11:13,297 --> 00:11:14,674
Maybe...

229
00:11:15,466 --> 00:11:19,303
they don't follow you because
they don't know who you really are.

230
00:11:19,387 --> 00:11:23,808
You always have your guard up,
you're kind of… a mystery.

231
00:11:24,934 --> 00:11:26,018
Right.

232
00:11:26,102 --> 00:11:28,145
You need to let them in.

233
00:11:29,146 --> 00:11:30,856
Hang out with them, you know.

234
00:11:31,357 --> 00:11:33,275
Show them the Cam that I know.

235
00:11:35,027 --> 00:11:36,028
How?

236
00:11:38,197 --> 00:11:41,659
Maybe we should go
to Fall Formal with them.

237
00:11:42,159 --> 00:11:43,536
Is this a promposal?

238
00:11:44,453 --> 00:11:47,998
You couldn't tell by the romantic tacos
with a side of blisters?

239
00:11:48,082 --> 00:11:49,750
It's perfect.

240
00:11:49,834 --> 00:11:51,585
[Teagan giggles]

241
00:11:52,920 --> 00:11:54,839
I don't know where I'm gonna find a suit.

242
00:11:55,339 --> 00:11:56,549
Well, we do know a guy.

243
00:11:57,675 --> 00:11:58,759
[catwalk music playing]

244
00:11:58,843 --> 00:12:00,136
So what are we feeling?

245
00:12:00,219 --> 00:12:04,223
Pedro Pascal Met Gala,
Paul Mescal swag, Bad Bunny big swing?

246
00:12:04,306 --> 00:12:06,100
What's the vibe? Right? What's resonating?

247
00:12:08,477 --> 00:12:12,189
-Nope. Mistakes made. I'm out.
-Whoa. Okay, hang on, look.

248
00:12:12,273 --> 00:12:14,483
You need to get out of your comfort zone.

249
00:12:15,359 --> 00:12:17,361
Perry, dial it back a bit.

250
00:12:17,445 --> 00:12:20,614
Sorry. I'm just really excited
to get rid of those chinos.

251
00:12:20,698 --> 00:12:21,949
Okay, okay.

252
00:12:23,033 --> 00:12:25,745
Look, a suit makes a man.

253
00:12:26,245 --> 00:12:28,247
Why don't you tell me
a bit about your style?

254
00:12:28,330 --> 00:12:30,332
Does it fit, and is it clean?

255
00:12:30,416 --> 00:12:31,417
Hm.

256
00:12:32,168 --> 00:12:36,756
Comfortable. Not showy, but… proud.

257
00:12:38,257 --> 00:12:39,383
Hang on.

258
00:12:40,551 --> 00:12:42,136
[whispering] Chu-chu-chu…

259
00:12:42,219 --> 00:12:43,429
Ah!

260
00:12:43,929 --> 00:12:46,474
-Here you are.
-[Teagan] Hm!

261
00:12:47,767 --> 00:12:49,769
Wait, how did you do that?

262
00:12:49,852 --> 00:12:52,146
Call it a gift. Suit up.

263
00:12:52,229 --> 00:12:54,023
[upbeat music playing]

264
00:12:54,106 --> 00:12:58,319
The designer sent some outfits for you
over with my dress so we match properly.

265
00:12:58,402 --> 00:13:00,738
I think you should wear this one.

266
00:13:00,821 --> 00:13:03,491
-Oh. Uh… Cool.
-Mm!

267
00:13:03,574 --> 00:13:05,409
As king and queen,

268
00:13:06,160 --> 00:13:08,621
we get a head table

269
00:13:08,704 --> 00:13:11,499
so we can invite the crew
to be our royal court

270
00:13:11,582 --> 00:13:14,752
with photos with them
scheduled before the dance.

271
00:13:14,835 --> 00:13:16,670
Ah, those guys are so photogenic.

272
00:13:16,754 --> 00:13:19,715
Then it's dinner, dancing, more photos,

273
00:13:19,799 --> 00:13:24,512
then finally
the king and queen slow dance.

274
00:13:24,595 --> 00:13:27,807
Wow, it sounds like you have
the whole day planned out.

275
00:13:27,890 --> 00:13:29,350
Well, yeah, babe, it's a big deal.

276
00:13:29,892 --> 00:13:32,645
Hey, do you think
we could hang before the dance?

277
00:13:32,728 --> 00:13:34,396
I just thought we could talk.

278
00:13:36,857 --> 00:13:38,984
There's just some things on my mind that…

279
00:13:39,985 --> 00:13:42,404
If we do that, I won't have time
for my hair appointment.

280
00:13:42,488 --> 00:13:44,365
And you know Alejandro
he hates being rushed.

281
00:13:44,448 --> 00:13:45,574
I know.

282
00:13:45,658 --> 00:13:47,660
Maybe we can later.

283
00:13:47,743 --> 00:13:49,495
-[knocking on door]
-Ooh.

284
00:13:49,578 --> 00:13:51,330
That might be the jeweler.

285
00:13:51,872 --> 00:13:53,249
-Hi.
-Mom.

286
00:13:53,332 --> 00:13:55,793
I thought we were going
to meet up at the dance.

287
00:13:55,876 --> 00:13:58,254
Oh, my Fall Formal Queen.

288
00:13:58,337 --> 00:14:00,256
[gasps] And her king.

289
00:14:00,339 --> 00:14:03,759
Lovely to see you, Senator Garner.
Did you get in okay from Beacon Hill?

290
00:14:03,843 --> 00:14:04,760
I got out early,

291
00:14:04,844 --> 00:14:08,639
so I thought maybe we could
squeeze in dinner and a mani-pedi.

292
00:14:08,722 --> 00:14:11,642
Sorry, Mom,
we're running on a tight schedule.

293
00:14:12,142 --> 00:14:13,352
I'll see you tomorrow?

294
00:14:15,145 --> 00:14:15,980
Uh…

295
00:14:16,063 --> 00:14:18,107
-All right, darling.
-Yeah. Okay.

296
00:14:18,607 --> 00:14:20,526
-Bye.
-[Josh] Take care.

297
00:14:21,068 --> 00:14:23,153
[Britney] Oh, we gotta take this in.

298
00:14:26,907 --> 00:14:28,993
[man] Yeah, I saw the deadline
on the notice.

299
00:14:29,660 --> 00:14:32,454
Look, I know we're a few months late.
It's a slow season.

300
00:14:32,538 --> 00:14:34,957
I just need a couple extra weeks.

301
00:14:36,876 --> 00:14:39,628
Okay, good. Thank you.

302
00:14:41,130 --> 00:14:43,340
-Dad, everything okay?
-Nothing to worry about.

303
00:14:43,424 --> 00:14:45,843
But your new school uniform
is gonna have to wait.

304
00:14:45,926 --> 00:14:47,636
You okay with the old one?

305
00:14:48,137 --> 00:14:49,388
Yeah, it's fine.

306
00:14:49,471 --> 00:14:52,266
And can you pitch in
on the evening shifts this week?

307
00:14:52,349 --> 00:14:54,101
-Yeah, of course.
-Great.

308
00:14:54,184 --> 00:14:57,730
Except for Friday.
I'm taking someone to Fall Formal.

309
00:14:57,813 --> 00:14:59,899
-Well, fantastic.
-Yeah, but, I mean, I could stay.

310
00:14:59,982 --> 00:15:02,651
No, no, absolutely not.
Who's the lucky date?

311
00:15:02,735 --> 00:15:04,653
Her name's Teagan. She's on crew.

312
00:15:04,737 --> 00:15:06,572
A girl after your own heart.

313
00:15:06,655 --> 00:15:08,282
Could I take the truck then?

314
00:15:09,241 --> 00:15:12,786
No. You can't take a girl
to a dance in that.

315
00:15:14,163 --> 00:15:17,166
I've got a client
who owes me a bit of a favor.

316
00:15:17,666 --> 00:15:20,252
You're gonna go in style.

317
00:15:20,336 --> 00:15:22,671
Come on. Check this out.

318
00:15:22,755 --> 00:15:25,841
["My Everything" by W.E.T. playing]

319
00:15:25,925 --> 00:15:28,302
<i>♪ Don't wanna let you down ♪</i>

320
00:15:28,928 --> 00:15:31,180
<i>♪ And I don't get excited ♪</i>

321
00:15:31,805 --> 00:15:34,892
<i>♪ Even for a minute that's too far ♪</i>

322
00:15:35,392 --> 00:15:38,938
<i>♪ You're my everything</i>
<i>Bigger than the stars ♪</i>

323
00:15:39,021 --> 00:15:42,232
<i>♪ What a thing to be where you are ♪</i>

324
00:15:42,775 --> 00:15:45,861
<i>♪ And you made me see</i>
<i>From the very start ♪</i>

325
00:15:45,945 --> 00:15:49,573
<i>♪ Nowhere I'd rather be</i>
<i>Than in your arms ♪</i>

326
00:15:53,118 --> 00:15:56,330
<i>♪ The love we share will let you know ♪</i>

327
00:16:01,460 --> 00:16:02,795
Is Coach Hayden in?

328
00:16:03,295 --> 00:16:05,005
He just stepped out to the boatsheds.

329
00:16:05,089 --> 00:16:06,131
Ah.

330
00:16:07,299 --> 00:16:08,968
Hey, do you have a moment?

331
00:16:09,593 --> 00:16:13,013
I actually have a coach problem
that I was hoping you could solve.

332
00:16:16,767 --> 00:16:18,018
Ow-ah!

333
00:16:18,102 --> 00:16:20,729
-Okay, careful, Mom.
-Stop squirming.

334
00:16:20,813 --> 00:16:22,564
Hurry, I'm getting picked up any minute.

335
00:16:22,648 --> 00:16:24,858
We wouldn't be rushing
if you hadn't gone rowing.

336
00:16:24,942 --> 00:16:26,193
He's a rower?

337
00:16:26,276 --> 00:16:27,611
Yeah.

338
00:16:28,278 --> 00:16:30,364
-You met Cam at the regatta.
-Oh.

339
00:16:30,447 --> 00:16:33,367
Right. Yeah, he seems very nice.

340
00:16:33,450 --> 00:16:34,952
You don't remember him, do you?

341
00:16:35,035 --> 00:16:37,579
Of course I do.
He was the one wearing the hat.

342
00:16:37,663 --> 00:16:40,082
-Yeah, they were all in hats, Mom.
-[laughing]

343
00:16:40,165 --> 00:16:42,334
All right, we're done here.

344
00:16:42,418 --> 00:16:43,919
[giggles]

345
00:16:44,003 --> 00:16:46,714
Time for the big reveal.

346
00:16:46,797 --> 00:16:47,756
Oh.

347
00:16:48,632 --> 00:16:50,926
-Oh?
-You look beautiful.

348
00:16:52,720 --> 00:16:53,846
Thanks, Mom.

349
00:16:54,346 --> 00:16:55,389
[vehicle approaching]

350
00:16:56,640 --> 00:16:57,725
Okay. He's here.

351
00:16:57,808 --> 00:17:00,102
-Goodness. Look at this.
-Okay.

352
00:17:01,603 --> 00:17:05,524
Hello, shoulders. Is your date Superman?

353
00:17:05,607 --> 00:17:07,317
Mom, stop!

354
00:17:13,991 --> 00:17:14,992
Okay.

355
00:17:17,870 --> 00:17:19,663
Wow, Teagan.

356
00:17:19,747 --> 00:17:20,873
Hi.

357
00:17:20,956 --> 00:17:21,957
Hi.

358
00:17:23,000 --> 00:17:24,501
-Ready to go?
-Yeah.

359
00:17:24,585 --> 00:17:27,254
Yeah. Are you guys
still good to give me a lift?

360
00:17:28,380 --> 00:17:29,381
Just kidding.

361
00:17:29,465 --> 00:17:31,925
She's not kidding. Okay, go!

362
00:17:32,009 --> 00:17:33,510
-Bye.
-Go, go, go!

363
00:17:33,594 --> 00:17:34,595
[laughing] Bye.

364
00:17:39,391 --> 00:17:41,560
And you can take over the coat check,

365
00:17:41,643 --> 00:17:44,813
and you can keep the feisty ones
out of the rose garden.

366
00:17:47,316 --> 00:17:49,693
Hi, sorry I'm late. I'm Teagan's mama.

367
00:17:51,153 --> 00:17:53,197
DeeDee Garner, is that you?

368
00:17:53,280 --> 00:17:55,449
-Ella Emerson, you're back in the cove.
-Yeah.

369
00:17:55,532 --> 00:17:57,618
And still on your own personal schedule.

370
00:17:57,701 --> 00:18:00,370
Well, I'm here to help now.

371
00:18:00,454 --> 00:18:03,373
-Let's find something for you to do.
-So what have you been up to?

372
00:18:03,457 --> 00:18:05,834
-It's been 20 years.
-Harvard, Yale for law.

373
00:18:05,918 --> 00:18:07,961
I'm a state senator now. How about you?

374
00:18:08,462 --> 00:18:12,508
Well, I got married
and then that ended, so…

375
00:18:12,591 --> 00:18:14,551
And that's what brought you back home.

376
00:18:14,635 --> 00:18:18,764
Yes, I've taken over my parents' place,
which has been a maintenance nightmare.

377
00:18:18,847 --> 00:18:22,684
But I think you know a thing or two
about heritage houses.

378
00:18:22,768 --> 00:18:24,978
I see you've been doing some research.

379
00:18:25,062 --> 00:18:28,440
I recently applied for a permit
to fix my plumbing,

380
00:18:28,524 --> 00:18:30,484
but it was denied
by the heritage committee,

381
00:18:30,567 --> 00:18:35,072
so I thought maybe there might be a way
for you to put a good word in for me.

382
00:18:35,155 --> 00:18:36,782
[laughs]

383
00:18:36,865 --> 00:18:37,866
I don't think so.

384
00:18:38,784 --> 00:18:40,828
Ah. Here we go.

385
00:18:40,911 --> 00:18:44,081
Looks like the punch table
could use some cups.

386
00:18:44,832 --> 00:18:46,416
You think you can handle cups?

387
00:18:46,500 --> 00:18:48,544
Sure, it's just cups.

388
00:18:49,586 --> 00:18:50,963
Friggin' cups.

389
00:18:53,924 --> 00:18:56,552
Hey, you guys. Since when do you DJ?

390
00:18:56,635 --> 00:18:58,428
He's not DJ-ing tonight, I am.

391
00:18:58,512 --> 00:19:00,722
Unless you want a two-hour set
of Nelly and Destiny's Child.

392
00:19:00,806 --> 00:19:03,517
-Hey, play nice.
-I can't wait to dance to your set.

393
00:19:03,600 --> 00:19:05,936
Your participation is not necessary.

394
00:19:06,019 --> 00:19:07,396
[Hayden] Maddy.

395
00:19:09,606 --> 00:19:10,649
Sorry about that.

396
00:19:10,732 --> 00:19:13,485
I'm gonna go try to find DeeDee
and see where I'm stationed.

397
00:19:13,569 --> 00:19:14,570
-See you.
-See you.

398
00:19:18,157 --> 00:19:20,659
So, I looked you up online.

399
00:19:20,742 --> 00:19:23,954
Okay, cool. Well, I have nothing to hide.

400
00:19:24,037 --> 00:19:29,418
This is true, there's not much there.
No school, no employment history, just…

401
00:19:30,002 --> 00:19:31,044
wife of a felon.

402
00:19:31,128 --> 00:19:34,798
And assistant manager
at the Crab Shack, probationary.

403
00:19:34,882 --> 00:19:36,967
Right, so I just wanna know,

404
00:19:37,050 --> 00:19:40,220
if you are pursuing my father,
what do you bring to the table?

405
00:19:42,639 --> 00:19:48,645
[upbeat music playing]

406
00:19:48,729 --> 00:19:52,399
[photographer] Okay, if I can have you
both just staring into each other's eyes.

407
00:19:53,275 --> 00:19:57,988
Fantastic, Britney.
Looking very presidential. Perfect.

408
00:20:07,831 --> 00:20:10,375
Next, just the queen and her mother.

409
00:20:12,711 --> 00:20:15,380
-Looking dapper.
-You too, man.

410
00:20:19,301 --> 00:20:21,428
The royal court has arrived.

411
00:20:21,511 --> 00:20:22,512
Oh!

412
00:20:22,596 --> 00:20:24,223
King of fashion over here.

413
00:20:24,306 --> 00:20:26,558
-[Josh] Pink-hair Perry!
-Boys.

414
00:20:26,642 --> 00:20:28,894
Come on, bro.

415
00:20:28,977 --> 00:20:29,811
Regis.

416
00:20:29,895 --> 00:20:32,105
-Dude, what is good, man?
-Good to see you, bro.

417
00:20:32,189 --> 00:20:33,315
[Amber] Hi, boys.

418
00:20:33,398 --> 00:20:35,817
-[Josh] You look beautiful.
-[Ryder] What happened to tie a tie?

419
00:20:35,901 --> 00:20:37,569
[Crabcatcher] Baloo, you clean up nice.

420
00:20:37,653 --> 00:20:39,404
-Crabby.
-[Noah] That's some suit, Baloo.

421
00:20:39,488 --> 00:20:41,281
What's up, man? Looking good.

422
00:20:41,365 --> 00:20:43,492
-[Perry] Hey, where's Cam?
-[Crabcatcher] Lookin' good.

423
00:20:43,575 --> 00:20:44,576
[Perry] Everyone's so fresh.

424
00:20:44,660 --> 00:20:46,703
["Poquito mas" by Kacy Hill playing]

425
00:20:50,332 --> 00:20:51,333
[Josh] Whoa.

426
00:20:53,585 --> 00:20:54,586
[Noah] Who's this?

427
00:21:00,634 --> 00:21:02,552
[all exclaiming]

428
00:21:02,636 --> 00:21:05,138
[Baloo] Come on! You look good.

429
00:21:05,222 --> 00:21:08,267
I did that. That was me. I'm a genius.

430
00:21:10,269 --> 00:21:11,270
Thanks, guys.

431
00:21:11,353 --> 00:21:13,021
Hey, who's the lucky date?

432
00:21:17,109 --> 00:21:19,569
<i>♪ Like seeing the signs</i>
<i>Now that it's over ♪</i>

433
00:21:20,988 --> 00:21:24,032
<i>♪ One, two at a time</i>
<i>Pushing me closer ♪</i>

434
00:21:25,826 --> 00:21:27,369
Yes!

435
00:21:29,121 --> 00:21:32,165
<i>♪ Time never lasts</i>
<i>Just like they told you ♪</i>

436
00:21:33,250 --> 00:21:36,086
<i>♪ Seeing the signs now that it's over ♪</i>

437
00:21:36,878 --> 00:21:40,716
<i>♪ Sometimes ♪</i>

438
00:21:40,799 --> 00:21:44,177
<i>♪ I still care ♪</i>

439
00:21:44,261 --> 00:21:46,471
Get out there. Come on.

440
00:21:46,972 --> 00:21:48,390
Bring it in.

441
00:21:50,017 --> 00:21:54,229
Hey, guys, we need photos of the court.
Let's head inside.

442
00:21:54,313 --> 00:21:55,564
-All right.
-Let's go.

443
00:21:55,647 --> 00:21:57,149
-This is it.
-Okay.

444
00:21:57,232 --> 00:21:59,276
-[Britney] You look nice.
-[Perry] Thanks.

445
00:22:01,320 --> 00:22:03,196
-Come on.
-Yeah.

446
00:22:09,161 --> 00:22:11,079
[Hayden] Welcome, everyone. Come on in.

447
00:22:15,959 --> 00:22:18,420
Please find your table, take your seats.

448
00:22:19,921 --> 00:22:21,381
[boy] Come over here, sit with me.

449
00:22:21,465 --> 00:22:23,925
[Britney] Okay. Can you hold this? Thanks.

450
00:22:25,552 --> 00:22:27,220
Here we go.

451
00:22:28,722 --> 00:22:30,849
Wow. And there we are.

452
00:22:30,932 --> 00:22:32,809
And the lapel.

453
00:22:32,893 --> 00:22:36,855
Josh and Britney,
it's time for the king and queen entrance.

454
00:22:37,397 --> 00:22:39,107
[both screaming]

455
00:22:39,191 --> 00:22:41,443
[Britney] Okay, okay. Hi.

456
00:22:43,153 --> 00:22:47,532
So, you and Cam. Looks official.

457
00:22:48,033 --> 00:22:51,370
If you can't say something nice,
shut the hell up.

458
00:22:51,453 --> 00:22:53,830
Okay, fair.

459
00:22:56,083 --> 00:22:58,794
You look great. Both of you.

460
00:22:59,336 --> 00:23:01,338
-[Hayden] Please welcome the royal court.
-Thank you.

461
00:23:01,421 --> 00:23:03,382
[Hayden] The senior boys' rowing team.

462
00:23:03,465 --> 00:23:05,967
[dramatic, upbeat music playing]

463
00:23:08,136 --> 00:23:10,806
-Please be seated for the entrance.
-Josh! We have to go.

464
00:23:10,889 --> 00:23:11,890
-Okay.
-Come.

465
00:23:11,973 --> 00:23:13,892
-All right!
-[student] Britney, I love you!

466
00:23:13,975 --> 00:23:18,647
And now, put your hands together
for your Fall Formal King and Queen,

467
00:23:18,730 --> 00:23:21,650
Britney Garner and Josh Regis.

468
00:23:21,733 --> 00:23:24,986
[upbeat music continues]

469
00:23:27,322 --> 00:23:28,490
Whoo!

470
00:23:31,326 --> 00:23:33,537
<i>♪ It doesn't matter ♪</i>

471
00:23:33,620 --> 00:23:36,415
<i>♪ I can't stop</i>
<i>It doesn't matter ♪</i>

472
00:23:37,457 --> 00:23:41,044
<i>♪ We're gon' fly</i>
<i>It doesn't matter ♪</i>

473
00:23:42,796 --> 00:23:44,881
<i>♪ It doesn't matter ♪</i>

474
00:23:44,965 --> 00:23:46,758
[sighs] Thank you.

475
00:23:46,842 --> 00:23:48,844
<i>♪ It doesn't matter ♪</i>

476
00:23:58,520 --> 00:23:59,354
[song ends]

477
00:24:02,482 --> 00:24:07,404
So, this orange thing is
"a compressed melon with micro basil."

478
00:24:07,988 --> 00:24:10,574
-How badly do you want a burger right now?
-[laughs]

479
00:24:11,366 --> 00:24:14,244
Cam Dillinger. Are you having fun?

480
00:24:14,870 --> 00:24:15,871
You caught me.

481
00:24:16,455 --> 00:24:17,497
[laughs]

482
00:24:17,581 --> 00:24:19,374
[Teagan and Cam laughing]

483
00:24:20,917 --> 00:24:24,004
Hey. The boys and I are going
for a donut run if you want in.

484
00:24:24,087 --> 00:24:25,547
I think it might be fun.

485
00:24:26,047 --> 00:24:28,550
There's no way
powdered sugar is going near this dress.

486
00:24:29,301 --> 00:24:32,929
And we are king and queen.
We cannot just leave.

487
00:24:33,013 --> 00:24:35,432
No one's gonna care
if we're gone for 20 minutes.

488
00:24:35,515 --> 00:24:36,600
I care.

489
00:24:37,142 --> 00:24:39,102
I don't wanna miss any part of our night.

490
00:24:43,982 --> 00:24:46,943
Do you think we'll ever be
the most popular ones at Easton?

491
00:24:48,320 --> 00:24:51,531
I think that with you
at the head of the dance committee

492
00:24:51,615 --> 00:24:56,536
and me in stroke seat
that… we can do anything.

493
00:24:57,621 --> 00:25:00,499
And now for a little something
to start the festivities.

494
00:25:00,582 --> 00:25:03,543
["Cursed Romantics"
by Maude Latour playing]

495
00:25:04,252 --> 00:25:05,170
Oh!

496
00:25:05,879 --> 00:25:08,048
-This is my jam.
-Let's boogie.

497
00:25:09,007 --> 00:25:11,343
-[Baloo] Come on, buddy. Let's go.
-Let's go.

498
00:25:12,177 --> 00:25:15,764
<i>♪ Baby, we're just cursed romantics ♪</i>

499
00:25:18,433 --> 00:25:21,811
Come on. The dance floor is calling us.

500
00:25:23,146 --> 00:25:25,315
-Come on. Let's go.
-Yeah.

501
00:25:27,359 --> 00:25:32,531
<i>♪ Oh damn, I hate this part</i>
<i>Violet delights have violent ends ♪</i>

502
00:25:32,614 --> 00:25:36,368
<i>♪ What do I do</i>
<i>When your love has changed me? ♪</i>

503
00:25:36,451 --> 00:25:39,871
<i>♪ It's so impressive</i>
<i>When you overtake me ♪</i>

504
00:25:39,955 --> 00:25:42,499
<i>♪ Your love is poison and nobody can… ♪</i>

505
00:25:42,582 --> 00:25:45,043
I know a way
you can really get the team behind you.

506
00:25:45,126 --> 00:25:46,711
-Yeah, what's that?
-Mm-hmm.

507
00:25:46,795 --> 00:25:49,005
-Show us your moves.
-Not happening.

508
00:25:49,089 --> 00:25:50,799
The whole team's out there.

509
00:25:51,591 --> 00:25:52,842
Come on.

510
00:25:53,927 --> 00:25:55,470
[Teagan giggles]

511
00:25:55,554 --> 00:25:57,222
It's fun.

512
00:25:57,305 --> 00:25:58,515
All right.

513
00:25:58,598 --> 00:26:01,393
<i>♪ We're just cursed romantics ♪</i>

514
00:26:01,476 --> 00:26:05,063
<i>♪ Tragedy, catastrophe ♪</i>

515
00:26:05,146 --> 00:26:08,733
<i>♪ Beautiful, so dramatic ♪</i>

516
00:26:08,817 --> 00:26:12,237
-[dance music playing]
-[people whooping and cheering]

517
00:26:12,320 --> 00:26:14,239
<i>♪ Let's make some arrangements ♪</i>

518
00:26:14,322 --> 00:26:17,701
<i>♪ Can I make your acquaintance?</i>
<i>That next-level dimension ♪</i>

519
00:26:17,784 --> 00:26:21,746
<i>♪ That's why I'm not to mention</i>
<i>Is that beyond your comprehension? ♪</i>

520
00:26:21,830 --> 00:26:25,667
<i>♪ Are you gonna come to the after party</i>
<i>To the after party, to the after party? ♪</i>

521
00:26:25,750 --> 00:26:27,460
<i>♪ Are you gonna come</i>
<i>'Cause I like to party ♪</i>

522
00:26:27,544 --> 00:26:29,462
<i>♪ 'Cause I like to party</i>
<i>'Cause I like to party ♪</i>

523
00:26:30,255 --> 00:26:33,341
<i>♪ To the after party</i>
<i>The after party, the after party ♪</i>

524
00:26:34,050 --> 00:26:36,219
<i>♪ 'Cause I like to party</i>
<i>'Cause I like to party ♪</i>

525
00:26:36,303 --> 00:26:40,432
<i>♪ You've got me so high</i>
<i>That I can't leave ♪</i>

526
00:26:41,266 --> 00:26:44,603
[different song playing]

527
00:26:44,686 --> 00:26:50,442
[all chanting] Go, Crabby! Go, Crabby!
Go, Crabby! Go, Crabby! Go, Crabby!

528
00:26:50,525 --> 00:26:53,403
[cheering]

529
00:26:58,199 --> 00:27:00,744
Go, Baloo! Go, Baloo!

530
00:27:03,413 --> 00:27:04,956
Work it, Baloo!

531
00:27:05,040 --> 00:27:07,375
[encouraging and cheering]

532
00:27:14,299 --> 00:27:15,842
Oh!

533
00:27:18,219 --> 00:27:21,097
-That's my cue to go get some punch.
-Whoa, nice try, Dillinger.

534
00:27:21,181 --> 00:27:22,349
It's almost your turn.

535
00:27:22,432 --> 00:27:24,517
No, no, I'm not going in there.
I'm terrible.

536
00:27:25,977 --> 00:27:28,688
Can't be worse
than Bert and Ernie over here.

537
00:27:30,815 --> 00:27:32,067
Quaid, put me down!

538
00:27:34,736 --> 00:27:39,032
Go, Perry! Let's go, Perry!

539
00:27:46,373 --> 00:27:48,541
Yeah, I'm not following that.

540
00:27:48,625 --> 00:27:50,835
Do you want to be stroke or not?

541
00:27:53,963 --> 00:27:54,964
Go!

542
00:27:59,552 --> 00:28:00,762
[Teagan] Whoo!

543
00:28:01,763 --> 00:28:04,474
-[boy] Yo, dance!
-[Teagan] Hey! Look at me.

544
00:28:05,934 --> 00:28:10,188
[all exclaiming and cheering]

545
00:28:17,529 --> 00:28:19,155
Whoa, Cam!

546
00:28:23,159 --> 00:28:25,078
[Quaid] Whoa, Cam!

547
00:28:25,161 --> 00:28:27,122
Did you know he could do that?

548
00:28:30,959 --> 00:28:33,670
-Hey, is everything okay?
-The air-conditioning shut off.

549
00:28:33,753 --> 00:28:36,715
We need to get it back on
before this room turns into a swamp.

550
00:28:36,798 --> 00:28:39,092
Okay, well, I could maybe call someone.

551
00:28:39,175 --> 00:28:40,844
I'm sure you maybe could.

552
00:28:41,636 --> 00:28:42,929
Why are you so mad?

553
00:28:45,974 --> 00:28:47,016
What did I do?

554
00:28:47,100 --> 00:28:51,771
It's not important.
Bet we tripped the breaker the AC is on.

555
00:28:52,439 --> 00:28:53,690
Ugh.

556
00:28:53,773 --> 00:28:54,691
Ah.

557
00:28:56,234 --> 00:28:58,069
And we have cool air.

558
00:28:58,153 --> 00:28:59,738
Just like that?

559
00:29:00,947 --> 00:29:01,948
What?

560
00:29:02,949 --> 00:29:04,784
Did you shut the door?

561
00:29:04,868 --> 00:29:06,369
-Uh…
-[doorknob rattling]

562
00:29:06,453 --> 00:29:08,204
We're trapped.

563
00:29:08,288 --> 00:29:13,168
God, I am in town for exactly 48 hours
to see my daughter's special moment.

564
00:29:13,251 --> 00:29:15,128
Now I'm going to miss it because of you.

565
00:29:15,211 --> 00:29:18,631
I'm really sorry, DeeDee.
It was an accident.

566
00:29:18,715 --> 00:29:20,633
It's never your fault, is it?

567
00:29:20,717 --> 00:29:22,969
Why do you have it in for me?

568
00:29:23,052 --> 00:29:25,221
Do you want to know what you did?

569
00:29:27,098 --> 00:29:28,141
You're helpless.

570
00:29:28,224 --> 00:29:31,644
Even back in our pageant days,
you always needed to bum a ride,

571
00:29:31,728 --> 00:29:34,564
or you'd forget your hairspray,
or need help with your dress.

572
00:29:35,064 --> 00:29:39,027
You were helpless, and you relied
on everyone else to put you together.

573
00:29:39,110 --> 00:29:43,823
You asked me, a state senator, for help
with a local permit. It's pathetic.

574
00:29:47,202 --> 00:29:48,203
Okay.

575
00:29:50,371 --> 00:29:52,332
You've said your piece.

576
00:29:59,380 --> 00:30:00,381
What are you doing?

577
00:30:00,882 --> 00:30:02,884
Getting us out of here.

578
00:30:06,638 --> 00:30:10,475
-Do you know what you're doing?
-Of course not.

579
00:30:15,605 --> 00:30:17,649
[lively music playing]

580
00:30:33,039 --> 00:30:35,792
Oh look, it's me if I had no taste.

581
00:30:35,875 --> 00:30:38,545
Oh look, it's me with no finesse.

582
00:30:40,213 --> 00:30:41,756
Walking away.

583
00:30:54,394 --> 00:30:56,729
-Mm!
-Tell her to change now.

584
00:30:56,813 --> 00:30:57,647
Who?

585
00:30:57,730 --> 00:30:59,691
Juliet. She's wearing my look.

586
00:30:59,774 --> 00:31:01,734
You're both making it work.

587
00:31:01,818 --> 00:31:03,319
I'm making it work better.

588
00:31:03,862 --> 00:31:05,280
You know, Perry,

589
00:31:05,780 --> 00:31:09,033
you've been clocking her all night
and for a while now.

590
00:31:09,117 --> 00:31:10,118
[scoffs]

591
00:31:10,201 --> 00:31:11,578
-Excuse me?
-Okay, come on.

592
00:31:11,661 --> 00:31:16,499
Has it ever occurred to you
that maybe you have a thing for her?

593
00:31:17,000 --> 00:31:21,379
Impossible. We fight all the time.
She's the Dior to my Coco Chanel.

594
00:31:21,462 --> 00:31:23,590
So maybe you finally met your match.

595
00:31:24,257 --> 00:31:26,634
What? No.

596
00:31:26,718 --> 00:31:29,679
You two kind of get each other
in a way that no one else does.

597
00:31:29,762 --> 00:31:32,140
That is… curious.

598
00:31:32,223 --> 00:31:35,977
Just go ask her to dance.
You know you want to. Go on.

599
00:31:36,895 --> 00:31:38,980
Last chance to get tickets
to the after-party.

600
00:31:39,647 --> 00:31:41,858
It's a charity cruise for the EPFA.

601
00:31:41,941 --> 00:31:45,904
Up for a romantic moonlit trip
through the Harbor Islands?

602
00:31:45,987 --> 00:31:48,072
Tickets are 250 each. Who's in?

603
00:31:48,865 --> 00:31:51,451
Yeah, put me down for two.
I got a hot date.

604
00:31:54,454 --> 00:31:57,373
-Anyone else? Noah, Cam?
-Sure.

605
00:32:00,418 --> 00:32:02,170
-Oh, um…
-I don't wanna go.

606
00:32:02,253 --> 00:32:03,338
We're having a good time.

607
00:32:03,421 --> 00:32:05,548
-I'm not dressed for the cold.
-[Perry] You should go.

608
00:32:06,215 --> 00:32:07,383
I'll take three.

609
00:32:07,467 --> 00:32:10,553
-Hey, come on. That's like 750 bucks.
-Don't worry about it.

610
00:32:10,637 --> 00:32:12,263
It's going to a good cause.

611
00:32:13,264 --> 00:32:15,016
Thanks, Perry.

612
00:32:16,935 --> 00:32:18,561
Let's go talk to them.

613
00:32:20,146 --> 00:32:24,067
See? You're making progress.
Even Perry's got your back.

614
00:32:28,071 --> 00:32:29,405
Do you know what the EPFA is?

615
00:32:30,657 --> 00:32:31,658
Should I?

616
00:32:31,741 --> 00:32:34,118
It's the Easton Prep
Financial Aid program.

617
00:32:34,202 --> 00:32:35,828
The one that goes to my tuition.

618
00:32:37,705 --> 00:32:39,165
I'm the good cause.

619
00:32:42,168 --> 00:32:43,252
Oh.

620
00:32:45,797 --> 00:32:47,715
Hey. Are you okay?

621
00:32:48,216 --> 00:32:49,926
Yeah, it's fine.

622
00:32:54,138 --> 00:32:55,932
You actually made it back.

623
00:32:56,015 --> 00:32:57,016
Huh!

624
00:33:00,645 --> 00:33:02,438
I apologize for getting short with you.

625
00:33:06,901 --> 00:33:08,152
It's fine.

626
00:33:11,656 --> 00:33:14,909
Actually, DeeDee, it's not fine.

627
00:33:15,576 --> 00:33:17,704
I know you think I'm flaky or whatever,

628
00:33:17,787 --> 00:33:20,581
but now I'm a single mother
to a teenage girl.

629
00:33:20,665 --> 00:33:23,418
For the last eight months,
I've had to be everything to her.

630
00:33:23,501 --> 00:33:26,587
And when something
needs to get done for her, I get it done.

631
00:33:26,671 --> 00:33:29,549
It doesn't matter how many vents
I need to crawl through

632
00:33:29,632 --> 00:33:32,218
or how many state senators I need to beg.

633
00:33:33,386 --> 00:33:34,679
Duly noted.

634
00:33:35,513 --> 00:33:38,808
Okay, great. Well, can you help me
get this permit approved, please?

635
00:33:40,309 --> 00:33:41,352
I'll see what I can do.

636
00:33:43,646 --> 00:33:46,441
You know, I spend most of the year
in Beacon Hill.

637
00:33:46,941 --> 00:33:49,736
When I come home,
my daughter acts like I'm invisible.

638
00:33:49,819 --> 00:33:51,612
It's like she hates me.

639
00:33:51,696 --> 00:33:53,698
Oh, well, my two cents,

640
00:33:53,781 --> 00:33:57,577
if it makes you feel any better,
she doesn't hate you. It's just…

641
00:33:58,870 --> 00:34:00,872
just how teenage girls are.

642
00:34:00,955 --> 00:34:02,206
You think so?

643
00:34:02,290 --> 00:34:05,835
Yeah, I'm stuck with mine all the time,
and it's the same.

644
00:34:06,544 --> 00:34:07,712
[both laughing]

645
00:34:08,379 --> 00:34:11,466
But once in a blue moon,
they need their moms.

646
00:34:11,966 --> 00:34:14,427
And you know what? You'll be there.

647
00:34:17,180 --> 00:34:19,682
[upbeat music playing]

648
00:34:28,858 --> 00:34:30,818
You really like this one, don't you?

649
00:34:30,902 --> 00:34:32,070
What gave it away?

650
00:34:32,153 --> 00:34:34,822
Your face. You forgot to be subtle.

651
00:34:37,700 --> 00:34:38,701
She seems okay.

652
00:34:39,202 --> 00:34:41,913
She is. A little more than okay.

653
00:34:43,581 --> 00:34:46,542
Listen, thanks for running defense
since your mom died.

654
00:34:46,626 --> 00:34:48,377
I know you've been looking out for me.

655
00:34:49,337 --> 00:34:51,881
Can you let this one through?

656
00:34:53,382 --> 00:34:55,134
I'll holster the glare.

657
00:34:55,802 --> 00:34:58,346
-Thank you. Okay. [laughing]
-For now.

658
00:35:09,774 --> 00:35:11,317
We could hit the dance floor.

659
00:35:15,321 --> 00:35:18,157
Or we can… just sit.

660
00:35:20,118 --> 00:35:21,119
Yeah.

661
00:35:25,289 --> 00:35:26,791
Cam, it's not a big deal.

662
00:35:27,834 --> 00:35:29,168
Yeah. Not to you.

663
00:35:29,252 --> 00:35:31,254
[emotional music playing]

664
00:35:32,338 --> 00:35:35,633
Look, you said I need to show them
who I am so they'll want to follow me.

665
00:35:35,716 --> 00:35:37,760
-Yeah.
-What am I supposed to show them?

666
00:35:38,427 --> 00:35:40,304
Hey, that I can't afford a new uniform?

667
00:35:40,805 --> 00:35:43,224
That I have to work shifts
at the shop after school?

668
00:35:44,475 --> 00:35:47,019
And their after-party
pays for my education.

669
00:35:47,645 --> 00:35:49,814
Is there anything in that
that someone wants to follow?

670
00:35:50,314 --> 00:35:52,817
Okay, they don't want to see that, Teagan.
No one does.

671
00:35:52,900 --> 00:35:55,236
-I do.
-Okay, but I don't want you to.

672
00:35:56,737 --> 00:35:59,532
Like, no matter what I do,
no matter how hard I row

673
00:35:59,615 --> 00:36:01,784
or how much I study
or how many shifts I work,

674
00:36:01,868 --> 00:36:04,162
I'm just always so far away
from being who I wanna be.

675
00:36:05,705 --> 00:36:07,748
-It's okay.
-No, it's not.

676
00:36:13,171 --> 00:36:16,549
Look, I don't think
I can do this right now.

677
00:36:20,303 --> 00:36:21,596
I'm sorry, Teagan.

678
00:36:35,234 --> 00:36:36,986
[Britney exclaiming]

679
00:36:37,069 --> 00:36:38,863
Look at the smolder on you.

680
00:36:38,946 --> 00:36:42,033
We are announcing
the king and queen dance in a few minutes.

681
00:36:42,116 --> 00:36:45,244
-Thank you.
-Okay, the last event of the night.

682
00:36:49,457 --> 00:36:52,877
What's the matter with you?
It's like you don't even wanna be here.

683
00:36:52,960 --> 00:36:55,004
I do.

684
00:36:55,713 --> 00:36:56,881
I just…

685
00:36:57,381 --> 00:37:01,177
When was the last time we actually talked?
Or just had fun together?

686
00:37:01,260 --> 00:37:04,722
I am having fun. Aren't you?

687
00:37:05,806 --> 00:37:06,807
No.

688
00:37:07,808 --> 00:37:08,809
Not really.

689
00:37:11,562 --> 00:37:14,065
I think we've been acting happy

690
00:37:14,148 --> 00:37:16,400
more than we've been happy
for a really long time.

691
00:37:16,484 --> 00:37:18,027
-Stop.
-Brit.

692
00:37:18,611 --> 00:37:21,948
Don't tell me you can't see it.
We don't want the same things.

693
00:37:22,031 --> 00:37:24,200
-And I'm not who you think I am.
-No.

694
00:37:25,660 --> 00:37:26,661
No.

695
00:37:27,912 --> 00:37:30,998
You are breaking up with me?

696
00:37:33,501 --> 00:37:34,502
Here?

697
00:37:35,878 --> 00:37:37,088
Now?

698
00:37:38,381 --> 00:37:40,675
I can't pretend anymore.

699
00:37:42,343 --> 00:37:43,511
I'm sorry.

700
00:37:44,512 --> 00:37:45,596
Is it Teagan?

701
00:37:46,222 --> 00:37:47,056
No.

702
00:37:48,057 --> 00:37:53,104
It's just that… this is over.

703
00:37:56,565 --> 00:37:59,068
[Hayden] And now it's time
for your king and queen

704
00:37:59,151 --> 00:38:02,238
-to lead with their first dance.
-[students cheering]

705
00:38:02,321 --> 00:38:03,614
[laughing]

706
00:38:03,698 --> 00:38:04,949
Awesome.

707
00:38:05,616 --> 00:38:08,536
Isn't that the perfect ending
to the article?

708
00:38:08,619 --> 00:38:10,454
"Alone and ditched on the dance floor."

709
00:38:10,538 --> 00:38:11,706
Thanks.

710
00:38:12,665 --> 00:38:14,583
-[music playing]
-[Hayden] Put your hands together

711
00:38:14,667 --> 00:38:18,045
for this year's reigning King and Queen
of the Fall Formal.

712
00:38:18,546 --> 00:38:21,674
-[clapping and cheering]
-["Slow Burn" By Anna Leanne playing]

713
00:38:23,384 --> 00:38:26,220
Hey. It doesn't have to end like that.

714
00:38:26,721 --> 00:38:29,598
Can I take you out for one last dance?

715
00:38:36,397 --> 00:38:42,653
<i>♪ I try to be the one you want</i>
<i>But, baby, I'm just scared ♪</i>

716
00:38:42,737 --> 00:38:46,574
Josh Regis and Britney Garner.

717
00:38:46,657 --> 00:38:52,747
<i>♪ 'Cause suddenly all the summers</i>
<i>Turn with you into lifetimes lately ♪</i>

718
00:38:52,830 --> 00:38:58,627
<i>♪ It feels like you are on fire</i>
<i>While it feels like a slow burn to me ♪</i>

719
00:38:59,253 --> 00:39:05,009
<i>♪ Guess that I'm not ready</i>
<i>Maybe I'm just scared ♪</i>

720
00:39:07,887 --> 00:39:11,515
<i>♪ I just need a little more time ♪</i>

721
00:39:13,059 --> 00:39:14,810
<i>♪ Am I falling ♪</i>

722
00:39:14,894 --> 00:39:20,775
<i>♪ Or making the same decision</i>
<i>That kept me from loving ♪</i>

723
00:39:20,858 --> 00:39:22,860
<i>♪ But it just led to nothing ♪</i>

724
00:39:24,111 --> 00:39:26,822
<i>♪ You're falling</i>
<i>I'm hating ♪</i>

725
00:39:26,906 --> 00:39:30,993
<i>♪ The way that I just</i>
<i>Always keep you waiting ♪</i>

726
00:39:31,952 --> 00:39:33,996
<i>♪ What if it's just… ♪</i>

727
00:39:34,080 --> 00:39:38,667
Look, if Cam can't get over himself,
that's his own problem.

728
00:39:38,751 --> 00:39:40,920
I just don't know what I did.

729
00:39:41,003 --> 00:39:42,088
Nothing.

730
00:39:42,171 --> 00:39:45,091
If he doesn't feel
like he's enough for you,

731
00:39:45,758 --> 00:39:47,176
there's nothing you can do.

732
00:39:48,511 --> 00:39:50,179
Only he can change that.

733
00:39:51,806 --> 00:39:52,848
Yeah.

734
00:39:52,932 --> 00:39:56,977
Want to bail? Watch <i>Saw </i>in my room?

735
00:39:58,145 --> 00:40:00,731
It'll be more romantic than this.

736
00:40:02,274 --> 00:40:04,360
Juliet, I have something to tell you.

737
00:40:05,277 --> 00:40:06,278
Your outfit.

738
00:40:08,197 --> 00:40:09,198
You wore it best.

739
00:40:10,866 --> 00:40:12,326
Would you like to dance?

740
00:40:15,204 --> 00:40:18,457
Yes. Go on. Come on.

741
00:40:18,541 --> 00:40:19,792
Go.

742
00:40:21,168 --> 00:40:23,003
I will kill you.

743
00:40:23,087 --> 00:40:24,463
You're welcome.

744
00:40:25,256 --> 00:40:29,760
<i>♪ What if it's just</i>
<i>Another lesson learned ♪</i>

745
00:40:29,844 --> 00:40:32,638
<i>♪ What if love is not a slow burn ♪</i>

746
00:40:38,310 --> 00:40:42,940
["Blonde" by Sunday (1994) playing]

747
00:40:58,706 --> 00:41:03,711
<i>♪ I was supposed to be the one… ♪</i>

748
00:41:03,794 --> 00:41:04,795
[DeeDee] Britney.

749
00:41:08,340 --> 00:41:09,508
I got you.

750
00:41:09,592 --> 00:41:12,052
<i>♪ My car won't start ♪</i>

751
00:41:12,136 --> 00:41:18,434
<i>♪ And I feel so old in this parking lot ♪</i>

752
00:41:18,934 --> 00:41:19,935
Ryder.

753
00:41:21,479 --> 00:41:24,398
Cabrera asked me to excuse you
from practice to meet with Dartmouth.

754
00:41:24,482 --> 00:41:28,152
I came to you first.
You left me no choice.

755
00:41:28,235 --> 00:41:31,739
So instead of prioritizing the team,
you decided to go over my head.

756
00:41:31,822 --> 00:41:33,324
Cabrera already said I could go.

757
00:41:33,407 --> 00:41:35,367
Which makes me think
you're not a serious leader.

758
00:41:36,035 --> 00:41:38,120
-It's her call.
-Here's mine.

759
00:41:38,621 --> 00:41:40,581
You are out of the stroke seat.

760
00:41:40,664 --> 00:41:41,707
Effective immediately.

761
00:41:41,790 --> 00:41:45,044
-But Coach--
-At the next regatta, we're starting Josh.

762
00:41:47,963 --> 00:41:50,674
<i>♪ I wanna be like her ♪</i>

763
00:41:50,758 --> 00:41:55,054
<i>♪ I wanna dye my hair… ♪</i>

764
00:41:59,391 --> 00:42:00,643
[Josh] Hey.

765
00:42:05,064 --> 00:42:06,357
What are you doing here?

766
00:42:06,440 --> 00:42:08,651
Um… [laughs]

767
00:42:10,819 --> 00:42:13,280
My night turned out to be a bust.

768
00:42:15,282 --> 00:42:17,743
-Is everything okay?
-Yeah. Uh…

769
00:42:22,081 --> 00:42:25,376
Turns out that Cam's not sure
he can do this right now.

770
00:42:25,918 --> 00:42:26,919
Oh.

771
00:42:27,920 --> 00:42:30,005
I'm sorry to hear that.

772
00:42:31,924 --> 00:42:33,676
What are you doing here?

773
00:42:34,552 --> 00:42:38,389
Uh, my night was also a bust.

774
00:42:39,473 --> 00:42:41,308
I broke up with Britney.

775
00:42:42,393 --> 00:42:44,019
Is that the right move?

776
00:42:46,522 --> 00:42:47,606
It was.

777
00:42:50,651 --> 00:42:53,237
Does that mean
she hates someone more than me now?

778
00:42:53,320 --> 00:42:54,738
[laughs]

779
00:42:54,822 --> 00:42:56,615
I think you're off the hook.

780
00:42:56,699 --> 00:43:00,327
Now I am the most hated person
on both of your lists.

781
00:43:00,411 --> 00:43:02,580
-[laughing]
-["Honeycrash" by Sasami playing]

782
00:43:02,663 --> 00:43:04,456
I don't hate you.

783
00:43:04,540 --> 00:43:07,209
<i>♪ Think about all the nights</i>
<i>You used to hold me ♪</i>

784
00:43:08,043 --> 00:43:11,547
<i>♪ Wonder why we couldn't make it out ♪</i>

785
00:43:12,715 --> 00:43:18,596
<i>♪ And who can love you ♪</i>

786
00:43:18,679 --> 00:43:24,476
<i>♪ Like I do right now ♪</i>

787
00:43:24,560 --> 00:43:27,313
<i>♪ Honey, don't count me out ♪</i>

788
00:43:27,855 --> 00:43:30,274
<i>♪ Even when the heavens sour ♪</i>

789
00:43:31,025 --> 00:43:34,153
<i>♪ Even in your darkest hour ♪</i>

790
00:43:34,236 --> 00:43:36,989
<i>♪ Even when the heart is cracked ♪</i>

791
00:43:37,489 --> 00:43:40,159
<i>♪ Honey, crash into me ♪</i>

792
00:43:40,242 --> 00:43:43,370
<i>♪ Like a storm into the sea ♪</i>

793
00:43:43,454 --> 00:43:46,582
<i>♪ Like blood on the silver screen ♪</i>

794
00:43:47,082 --> 00:43:49,627
<i>♪ We can make it through all that ♪</i>

795
00:43:51,545 --> 00:43:55,257
<i>♪ Looking for someone</i>
<i>To help me forget it ♪</i>

796
00:43:55,341 --> 00:43:59,011
<i>♪ Even though I know I'll regret it ♪</i>

797
00:43:59,637 --> 00:44:02,806
<i>♪ Hoping you change your mind ♪</i>

798
00:44:04,058 --> 00:44:10,022
<i>♪ And who can love you ♪</i>

799
00:44:10,105 --> 00:44:15,527
<i>♪ Like I do right now ♪</i>

800
00:44:16,403 --> 00:44:19,531
<i>♪ And if you leave ♪</i>

801
00:44:19,615 --> 00:44:22,534
<i>♪ It better be ♪</i>

802
00:44:22,618 --> 00:44:28,582
<i>♪ 'Cause you found someone</i>
<i>Who can love you better than me ♪</i>

803
00:44:28,666 --> 00:44:31,585
<i>♪ Honey, don't count me out ♪</i>

804
00:44:31,669 --> 00:44:34,838
<i>♪ Even when the heavens sour ♪</i>

805
00:44:34,922 --> 00:44:38,634
<i>♪ Even in your darkest hour ♪</i>

806
00:44:38,717 --> 00:44:40,719
[song ends]
